2	//!
3	//! Handles inline code spans, emphasis (bold/italic), links, images, line breaks, and raw HTML.
4	//!
5	//! # CommonMark Specification References
6	//!
7	//! This module implements the following CommonMark 0.31.2 sections:
8	//!
9	//! - **§6.1 Code spans**: Backtick-delimited inline code (`code`)
10	//! - **§6.2 Emphasis and strong emphasis**: `*italic*`, `**bold**`, `_italic_`, `__bold__`
11	//! - **§6.3 Links**: `[text](url)` inline links
12	//! - **§6.4 Autolinks (URI)**: `<https://example.com>`
13	//! - **§6.5 Autolinks (email)**: `<user@example.com>`
14	//! - **§6.6 Hard line breaks**: Trailing spaces or backslash before newline
15	//! - **§6.7 Soft line breaks**: Single newline within paragraph
16	//! - **§6.8 Raw HTML**: `<tag>`, `</tag>`, `<!-- comment -->`, `<?...?>`, `<!...>`, `<![CDATA[...]]>`
17	//!
18	//! # Emphasis Algorithm (§6.4)
19	//!
20	//! This module implements the CommonMark delimiter stack algorithm for emphasis:
21	//!
22	//! 1. **First pass**: Collect delimiter runs from the inline content
23	//! 2. **Second pass**: Match openers and closers using the delimiter stack algorithm
24	//! 3. **Rule of 3**: If (opener_count + closer_count) % 3 == 0 and both can open/close,
25	//!    skip the match unless both counts are divisible by 3
26	//!
27	//! # Emphasis Flanking Rules (§6.2)
28	//!
29	//! A delimiter run is **left-flanking** if:
30	//! 1. Not followed by Unicode whitespace, AND
31	//! 2. Not followed by punctuation, OR preceded by whitespace/punctuation
32	//!
33	//! A delimiter run is **right-flanking** if:
34	//! 1. Not preceded by Unicode whitespace, AND
35	//! 2. Not preceded by punctuation, OR followed by whitespace/punctuation
36	//!
37	//! Underscore (`_`) has additional intraword restrictions (§6.2 rules 2, 5, 7, 8).
